<main class="lg">
  <h1>Security and vulnerability disclosure</h1>
  <p class="lg-updated">Last updated November 15, 2026</p>

  <p>Schools trust Managira with student records, so we welcome reports from anyone who finds a security weakness in our service. This page explains how to report one, what we ask of you, and what you can expect from us.</p>

  <div class="lg-box">
    <strong>Report a security problem:</strong> email <a href="mailto:security@managira.com">security@managira.com</a> with a description, the steps to reproduce it, and the address or page involved. Please do not include student or family information in your report.
  </div>

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The page, address or feature affected, and the kind of problem (for example, access to another school's records).</li>
    <li>Step-by-step instructions to reproduce it, with screenshots or a short recording if they help.</li>
    <li>What an attacker could do with it, as you understand it.</li>
    <li>How we can reach you, and whether you would like to be credited once it is fixed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our commitments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We acknowledge your report within 3 business days and tell you who is handling it.</li>
    <li>We keep you informed as we confirm and fix the problem, and tell you when it is resolved.</li>
    <li>We fix confirmed problems as quickly as their severity requires, and notify affected schools as described in our <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li>We will not take legal action against research carried out in good faith under this policy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Guidelines for research</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Test only with accounts you own or have permission to use, and stop as soon as you reach data that is not yours.</li>
    <li>Do not view, change, download or delete other people's information, and do not keep any you encounter.</li>
    <li>Do not run denial-of-service tests, send spam, or use social engineering or physical attacks against our staff, schools or families.</li>
    <li>Do not use automated scanners in a way that degrades the service for schools.</li>
    <li>Give us reasonable time to fix a problem before you share details publicly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Managira does not run a paid bug bounty program at this time.</p>

  <h2>How we protect school data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All connections use HTTPS. Data is encrypted at rest, and nightly backups are encrypted before they are stored.</li>
    <li>Schools give each person a role and specific permissions, checked on our servers for every request. One school can never see another school's records.</li>
    <li>Passwords are stored only as salted hashes. Password sign-ins are confirmed with a code, by email or from an authenticator app, and schools can require an authenticator app or sign-in through their own identity provider.</li>
    <li>Student files open only through links that expire within minutes.</li>
    <li>Our full commitments are in the <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, and the services we use are listed on the <a href="/legal/subprocessors">subprocessors</a> page.</li>
  </ul>
</main>
